            <ArticleTitle>[Central neuroaxial blocade and metabolic stress-answer in a newborn and babies in surgical diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>58-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Investigation of markers of humoral stress was conducted in 25 babies (the main group), in whom a central neuroaxial blocade was performed while doing various surgical interventions. In a control group there were included 20 babies, in whom a standard atharalgesia was applied. The best efficacy was achieved while anesthesia using central neuroaxial blocade.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
